Test rg48: an origin's statement after each kind of statement
// Whatever precedes an origin line, that line is a new statement: its slash
// must not be taken for a divide continuing the last directive's operands.
// Each origin line puts a word at a new address, so a divide instead of an
// origin shows as a word at the wrong place.
100/ cla
    text "ab"
110/ 1
    ascii "AB"
120/ 2
    flexo 12
130/ 3
    type340 "AB"
140/ 4
    char 1r
150/ 5
    table 2, 7
160/ 6
    lac [17
170/ 7
    var q=3
    lac q
/* a C comment
   over two lines */
200/ 010
    lac 17          // an operand is not an origin
210/ 011
    hlt
220/ 012
    variables
    constants
stop
